### Run shop.http first so an order exists and has shipped, then request a return for one book
POST {{host}}/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": {{orderId}}, "sku": "BOOK-1", "quantity": 1 }

> {% client.global.set("returnId", response.body.id); %}

### Approve it
POST {{host}}/returns/{{returnId}}/approval

### The parcel arrived
POST {{host}}/returns/{{returnId}}/receipt

### Refund
POST {{host}}/returns/{{returnId}}/refund

### A second return of the same book, now refused (409): only one shipped
POST {{host}}/returns
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": {{orderId}}, "sku": "BOOK-1", "quantity": 2 }

### Look at the return
GET {{host}}/returns/{{returnId}}

### Returns rate per SKU
GET {{host}}/reports/returns-rate
